# jobhunt workspace — notes for Claude

This is a personal jobhunt *workspace* (profile, CV, ratings, digests). The code lives in the
`jobhunt` package installed from `pyproject.toml`. Everything here is personal data — never
publish it.

- `/jobhunt` runs the pipeline and records chat ratings — use it rather than scoring listings
  yourself.
- `uv run jobhunt serve` runs a local browser UI for the same pipeline; ratings made there land
  in `data/ratings.jsonl` like `jobhunt rate` does.
- Scoring and preference learning go through the shell `claude` CLI (`claude -p`); if it reports
  `OAuth session expired`, the user has to run `claude login`.
- Never work around scraper blocks (403/CAPTCHA/sign-in walls) — surface the manual link instead.
- Engine bugs or new sources belong in the engine repo, not here.
